NAME
       qsort, bsearch - sort and search an array

SYNOPSIS
       #include <stdlib.h>

       void  qsort(void *base, size_t n, size_t size,
                   int (*cmp)(const void *, const void *));
       void *bsearch(const void *key, const void *base, size_t n,
                     size_t size, int (*cmp)(const void *, const void *));

DESCRIPTION
       Sorts an array in place, and searches one that is already
       sorted. CMP returns a negative number, zero or a positive number
       as the first argument sorts before, equal to, or after the
       second.

RETURN VALUE
       bsearch returns a pointer to a matching element, or NULL.

SEE ALSO
       string(3), sort(1)
